[561.315333, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@e6a5710973d1:~/druid# "]
[579.611532, "i", "cat > /root/patches/README.md << 'EOF'\n# Apache Druid 0.20.0 JavaScript Code Execution Vulnerability Fix\n\n## Vulnerability Description\n\nAuthenticated attackers could execute arbitrary code on the server through malicious JavaScript payloads by bypassing JavaScript security settings using an empty key (\"\") in JSON requests.\n\nExample exploit:\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"index\",\n  \"spec\": {\n    \"dataSchema\": {\n      \"transformSpec\": {\n        \"filter\": {\n          \"type\": \"javascript\",\n          \"function\": \"function(){java.lang.Runtime.getRuntime().exec('malicious_command');}\",\n          \"\": {\n            \"enabled\": true\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe vulnerability existed because Jackson could deserialize JavaScriptConfig objects from user-provided JSON payloads, allowing attackers to override the system-injected configuration and enable JavaScript execution even when it was disabled at the system level.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nThe fix prevents JavaScriptConfig from being deserialized from user-provided JSON by:\n\n1. Adding `@JsonIgnore` annotation to the `config` field in all JavaScript-enabled classes\n2. Adding validation to ensure the config is properly injected and not null\n\n## Patched Files\n\n1. **JavaScriptDimFilter.java** - Filter for JavaScript-based dimension filtering\n2. **JavaScriptAggregatorFactory.java** - Aggregator using JavaScript functions\n3. **JavaScriptPostAggregator.java** - Post-aggregator using JavaScript functions\n4. **JavaScriptParseSpec.java** - Parser specification using JavaScript\n5. **JavaScriptWorkerSelectStrategy.java** - Worker selection strategy using JavaScript\n6. **JavaScriptExtractionFn.java** - Extraction function using JavaScript\n\n## Changes Made\n\nFor each vulnerable class:\n- Added `@JsonIgnore` annotation to the `JavaScriptConfig config` field\n- Added validation: `Preconditions.checkNotNull(config, \"JavaScriptConfig must be injected, not provided via JSON\")`\n\nThis ensures that:\n- The config field cannot be deserialized from user JSON\n- The config must come from system injection via Guice\n- Any attempt to provide config via JSON will fail validation\n\n## Build Information\n\nBuilt with Maven using:\n```bash\nmvn clean package -DskipTests -Dcheckstyle.skip=true -Dpmd.skip=true \\\n  -Dforbiddenapis.skip=true -Dspotbugs.skip=true -Danimal.sniffer.skip=true \\\n  -Denforcer.skip=true -Djacoco.skip=true -Ddependency-check.skip=true \\\n  -pl '!web-console' -pl indexing-service -am\n```\n\nOutput JAR: `/root/druid/indexing-service/target/druid-indexing-service-0.20.0.jar`\nEOF\n"]
